WEBVTT

00:02:29.246 --> 00:02:32.516
"having qualities that bring about
a favorable regard,

00:02:32.549 --> 00:02:34.818
pleasant or agreeable."

00:02:34.818 --> 00:02:36.586
The Urban Dictionary says:

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:40.090
"likeable, an adjective meaning
pleasant or attractive.

00:02:40.123 --> 00:02:43.126
It describes something
that is easy to like."

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:48.732
The sad truth is, most of us don't find
strong, competent women easy to like.

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:53.103
In 2003, Professor Flynn
at Columbia Business School

00:02:53.136 --> 00:02:54.938
conducted an experiment.

00:02:54.938 --> 00:02:57.307
He took a case study about Heidi Roizen,

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.710
a successful female venture capitalist,

00:02:59.743 --> 00:03:02.446
and he changed the name to Howard Roizen.